ive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the count-based selection with the fold's horizon guard: either count only foldable (older-than-horizon) live events for selection, or specify that a selected-but-nothing-to-fold ticket is not counted as compacted, so the sweep converges and reports accurately.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'select any ticket whose live count exceeds compact.threshold ... whether or not a SNAPSHOT is present'","compact_txn.py:365 'old = [... if is_foldable(ts, now, horizon)]' and 368-370 'if not old: ... nothing to fold ... return 0' — the fold does work only on older-than-horizon events, not on raw live count","compact_all_cli counts rc==0 as 'compacted += 1' (compact.py:255-256), so a no-op fold is reported as a compaction"],"finding":"The proposed selection predicate (raw live-event count > compact.threshold) diverges from the fold engine's actual work criterion, which only folds events OLDER than the horizon (compact_txn.py:365-370). An already-snapshotted ticket whose live count exceeds threshold but whose excess events are all within the compaction horizon will be selected every sweep, perform no folding (the fold returns rc==0 'all events within the compaction horizon — nothing to fold'), be counted as 'compacted', and be re-selected on the next run — a non-converging churn condition with a misleading compacted count.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdd5d24975d36e185","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section, item 1 (threshold-based selection) and compact_txn.py:352-370","norm_id":"n4b19229cd6986220","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["A high-traffic ticket already snapshotted accumulates many events all newer than the horizon; the sweep selects it every run but folds nothing and reports it compacted","Repeated sweeps never reduce the ticket, defeating the 'recurring sweep' goal for hot tickets"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2357,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The Testing section lists a 'Failure path' (rejected push leaves clone commits intact and reports failure) but there is no corresponding Acceptance Criterion, so this described deliverable has no covering criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fda96b6e298861373","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing 'Failure path' vs Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"nebb82e6b1438a918","priority":0.7143,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add AC: '[ ] A sweep whose push is rejected reports the failure and leaves the clone's commits intact — a test asserts non-corrupting behavior and a failure exit/summary.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification"